jros2: keep the instance of a keyless topic in DataReaderHistory::data_available_instances_

Fast-DDS 3.6.2 erases the (only, fictitious) instance of a keyless topic from data_available_instances_ whenever a
read/take leaves it without samples, and add_to_instance() re-inserts it when the next sample arrives. That is one
std::map node allocation (operator new, 72 bytes) on the receiving thread (transport receive thread, or the writer's
thread with intraprocess delivery) and one free on the taking thread for every sample a drained reader receives.
The constructor already keeps the empty instance available, so this only restores that state.

diff --git a/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/history/DataReaderHistory.cpp b/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/history/DataReaderHistory.cpp
index 7a2a2d3..aaf2124 100644
--- a/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/history/DataReaderHistory.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/fastdds/subscriber/history/DataReaderHistory.cpp
@@ -696,6 +696,14 @@ void DataReaderHistory::check_and_remove_instance(
             instances_.erase(instance_info->first);
         }
 
+        if (!has_keys_)
+        {
+            // The single (fictitious) instance of a keyless topic stays available, as after construction: erasing it
+            // here made add_to_instance() insert (allocate) a new map node for every sample that arrives after a
+            // read/take emptied the reader. Iterating an empty instance just yields no samples.
+            return;
+        }
+
         instance_info = data_available_instances_.erase(instance_info);
     }
 }
